 "cannot_emulate": [
  {
   "baseline": "semantic / embedding cache",
   "why_not": "The corpus stores parsed (tool, arguments) pairs only. There are no argument embeddings, no similarity scores and no threshold anywhere in the record, and no model is reachable offline. Reconstructing equivalence classes would mean choosing an embedder, a distance metric and a threshold -- three free parameters that are ours, not the workload's -- so any hit rate would measure our reconstruction, not the cache. It is also non-deterministic across embedder versions, which the paper's reproducibility discipline forbids."
  },
  {
   "baseline": "provider prefix cache (Anthropic/OpenAI prompt caching)",
   "why_not": "A prefix cache keys on the serialized prompt prefix of a model call (system prompt + message history) and bills input tokens as cache reads. The trace keeps neither the prompt text, nor token counts, nor prefix boundaries, nor per-call timestamps, so prefix identity, the minimum cacheable prefix (1024/2048 tokens) and the 5-minute TTL are all unobservable. It also saves input-token cost, not calls: it is a different denominator from the 41.70% call-level hit rate, and converting between them would require re-tokenizing reconstructed prompts -- invention. The paper therefore reports provider prefix caching only under a MODELED pricing overlay on measured tokens, which this corpus also lacks."
  },
  {
   "baseline": "capacity in bytes / TTL-based locality",
   "why_not": "Tool *results* are absent from the corpus, so entry sizes are unknown; capacity is therefore modeled in entries, not bytes. Timestamps are absent too, so time-to-live and inter-arrival locality cannot be evaluated; the LRU sweep is a logical-access ordering, not a wall-clock trace."
  },
  {
   "baseline": "end-to-end latency or dollar savings",
   "why_not": "No latency, token or price fields exist in the corpus. Hit rates are the only defensible offline output; any cost claim would need a pricing overlay plus measured tokens, neither of which is here."
  }
 ]
